From: Thorch maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: qcom: map SM8550 maximum UniPro clock to HS-G5

SM8550's UniPro clock and OPP tables top out at 300 MHz. Mapping that
frequency to HS-G4 prevents this controller from scaling back to HS-G5,
although the original Android implementation uses HS-G5 at its maximum
300 MHz clock. Limit the correction to the SM8550 compatible and retain
the negotiated device maximum clamp. Other controllers are unchanged.

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2540,7 +2540,12 @@ static u32 ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed(struct ufs_hba *hba, unsigned long freq)
 		gear = UFS_HS_G5;
 		break;
 	case 300000000:
-		gear = UFS_HS_G4;
+		/* SM8550 supports HS-G5 at its maximum 300 MHz UniPro clock.
+		 * Keep the newer-controller 403 MHz mapping for other SoCs.
+		 */
+		gear = of_device_is_compatible(hba->dev->of_node,
+					      "qcom,sm8550-ufshc") ?
+			UFS_HS_G5 : UFS_HS_G4;
 		break;
 	case 201500000:
 		gear = UFS_HS_G3;
